-- The rest of the world's zone points.
--
-- Importing the Atlantis rows turned up how deep the hole went: the dump
-- holds 1667 unique (Id, Realm) jump points and we had 269. Dungeon mouths
-- and dungeon exits all over the world were dead the same way Atlantis was
-- -- Stonehenge Barrows, Tomb of Mithra, Catacombs of Cardova, Keltoi Fogou,
-- Spindelhalla, Vendo Caverns, Nisse's Lair, Varulvhamn, Cursed Tomb, Muire
-- Tomb, Spraggon Den, Koalinth Tribal Caverns, Treibh Caillte, Tepok's Mine
-- and more, plus the 338 rows that carry you back out to Albion, Midgard and
-- Hibernia.
--
-- Two corrections were needed on the way in. The dump names the code-side
-- jump handlers DOL.GS.Scripts.*; in this server they live in
-- DOL.GS.ServerRules, and a ClassType that does not resolve logs an error and
-- drops the jump, so those are rewritten. And rows are left out rather than
-- imported broken: nine point at regions 3, 1007 and 1008, which this
-- database does not have, and ten name Catacombs adventure-wing handlers
-- (TheArena, LairOfDoom, BetrayersDen, RitualHall, HiddenCrypt,
-- HallOfReawakening, DeliahsSanctuary, LostWing, BeastmastersDen,
-- GoblinsCookery) that do not exist in OpenDAoC.
--
-- Nothing here collides with a row we already had, so no existing jump
-- changes behaviour.

